		(uuid "d6dd13b6-a4cd-595f-a96f-43be57186359")
	)
	(text "DRAFT – for ET review. Software: proto/port/linux/ui.c (inputs active low with the Pi's pull-ups; LEDs active high).\nMode switch (J12, ON-OFF-ON): GPIO 23 low = NM, else GPIO 16 low = MRM, else (centre) SRI. Role (J11): low = TX.\nPull-ups: the Pi's own (ui.c); rev A's external 10 kΩ are gone in rev B (one copper layer). 1 kΩ series: GPIO 16 may be driven by legacy firmware at boot\n(HAT design guide); 1 kΩ limits that to 3.3 mA into a closed switch. A TVS per lead right at the connectors.\nPanel holes: Ø7.5 mm for the PS1024 button, Ø6.5 mm for the 100-series toggles.\nGlue the XH housings to the board and the leads to the box (drop test)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 27.94 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b8757cfb-8700-5923-b3ba-21c65bd62d3d")
	)
	(text "CONNECTORS (panel parts off-board)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 81.28 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f7fbe73d-e134-5394-814e-cc088bd61a32")
	)
	(text "J10: panel button E-Switch PS1024ABLK (momentary).\nBench: plug the panel button into J10 (or bridge its two pins); no on-board button.\nJ11: role toggle E-Switch 100SP1T1B1M1QEH, closed = TX;\n  may stay unfitted until Atenea Q8 (open = RX).\nJ12: mode toggle E-Switch 100SP3T1B1M1QEH ON-OFF-ON:\n  1 NM, 2 common (GND), 3 MRM; centre = SRI."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 182.88 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "5c5871aa-4313-5887-94c9-d0ea7d57b9ea")
	)
	(text "NO EXTERNAL PULL-UPS IN REV B (R50-R53 of rev A)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 134.62 81.28 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "156a044a-61ff-56fe-9e50-e01eb6e0f497")
	)
	(text "The inputs use the Pi's pull-ups, which ui.c requests (GPIO_V2_LINE_FLAG_BIAS_PULL_UP) before it reads\nthem. Until then (boot) the BCM2837 default pull-down makes an open toggle read 'active' - nothing reads\nthem then. On one copper layer a 3V3 bus to four pull-ups at the leads cuts the ground pour into islands."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 134.62 86.36 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "2fa92ac8-d3f9-5291-9fc6-eef91fb347f4")
	)
